# slickrails: CODEOWNERS (rule 5) — who must review changes to sensitive paths.
#
# The AI review judges every PR, but someone who builds with an agent often cannot judge the verdict. For the
# paths below a named engineer should approve, whatever the AI said. Every line is commented out on purpose:
# replace the paths with your repo's own and @your-org/your-team with real GitHub users or teams, then remove the #.
# It only blocks merges once branch protection asks for it:  CODEOWNER_REVIEWS=1 slickrails protect
# A solo developer cannot approve their own PR — leave this off until there is a second person.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Authentication, sessions, permissions
# /src/auth/                        @your-org/your-team
# /src/**/permissions*              @your-org/your-team

# Payments and billing
# /src/billing/                     @your-org/your-team

# Database migrations and schema
# /migrations/                      @your-org/your-team
# /prisma/schema.prisma             @your-org/your-team

# Infrastructure, deployment, CI
# /infra/                           @your-org/your-team
# /.github/workflows/               @your-org/your-team

# The guardrails themselves
# /.slickrails/                     @your-org/your-team
# /.githooks/                       @your-org/your-team
# /.github/CODEOWNERS               @your-org/your-team
